# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# The simulation runs in web workers over SharedArrayBuffer, which browsers
# only expose to cross-origin-isolated documents. Without these two headers
# `arrayBuffer()` silently falls back to a plain ArrayBuffer, the workers
# mutate copies, and the wall renders but never moves.
#
# `require-corp` works in every browser, Safari included. It only allows
# cross-origin files that opt in, which is fine here: every image and data file
# is served from this site, and the two outside requests (Google Fonts and the
# detect-gpu benchmark on unpkg) both send
# `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin`. Upstream needed
# `credentialless` plus an iOS middleware only because it hotlinked TMDB images.
#
# No Pages Function is involved, so requests do not count against the Workers
# free-plan daily limit.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

# Hashed asset filenames change whenever content changes, so they can be
# cached indefinitely.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
